Package: tolome-artwork
Architecture: all
Depends: libglib2.0-0t64, libglib2.0-bin, pipewire-bin, plymouth, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: gnome-shell
Description: Visual identity of Tolome (wallpapers, icon, boot splash)
 Installs the Tɔlɔmɛ identity:
  * eight wallpapers of Benin, listed in the GNOME appearance settings,
    with Ganvié as the default wallpaper and lock screen background;
  * the Tɔlɔmɛ icon in the hicolor theme, named "tolome";
  * a Plymouth boot splash theme and a GRUB theme using the Tɔlɔmɛ logo
    on an indigo background;
  * a short login sound, played once at each GNOME login (not in the live
    session); it respects the user's volume and mute and can be disabled.
 .
 The defaults are set through a GSettings override and the Plymouth theme
 is selected with plymouth-set-default-theme; files of other packages are
 never modified.
